# MORE INFORMATION REQUIRED -> BORROWER REPLY -> OFFICER REVIEW
# Files were only read/edited. No build, service, API, Oracle or UI tests were run.
# Rebuild/restart Exit Service yourself; reload the frontend. Existing gateway
# routes and borrower/officer JWT guards cover these new endpoints unchanged.
# No schema migration or seeder reset is needed. Existing request 21 can be used
# if it is still MORE_INFO_REQUIRED, assigned, and its loan is ACTIVE, with no
# accepted/paid settlement for that request. Do not force statuses through SQL.
#
# CREATED
# Exit Service: service/RequestInformationService.java,
# controller/RequestInformationController.java, controller/RequestInformationErrors.java,
# request-information-manual.http
# Frontend: components/RequestInformation.jsx
# MODIFIED
# Frontend: api.js, officerApi.js, pages/BorrowerDashboard.jsx, pages/OfficerDashboard.jsx
#
# STORAGE / BUSINESS RULES
# Reuses COOLING_OFF_REQUEST + AUDIT_LOG only.
# Existing officer decisions already write COOLING_OFF_MORE_INFO_REQUIRED and the
# requested clarification in AUDIT_LOG.DETAILS; it is now visible in both dashboards.
# Responses write COOLING_OFF_INFO_SUBMITTED with USER_ID, ENTITY_ID=request ID,
# ENTITY_TYPE=COOLING_OFF_REQUEST, EXIT_REQUEST_ID and the trimmed reply in DETAILS.
# History exposes only those two action types after existing ownership/visibility
# checks. No unrelated financial/internal audit data or personal IDs are returned.
# Submission locks the owned request, requires MORE_INFO_REQUIRED and ACTIVE loan,
# assigned officer, and no accepted/paid settlement or successful payment for it.
# Status -> UNDER_REVIEW, UPDATED_AT -> current DB timestamp, DECIDED_AT -> NULL.
# Assigned officer, original reason, REQUEST_DATE, EXPIRY_DATE and CREATED_AT stay
# unchanged. Original decision questions/timestamps remain in audit history.
# History and status changes commit together; repeated/stale submissions return 409
# without adding another reply. Wrong borrower/request returns 404; wrong role is
# denied. Blank/oversized responses return 400; unavailable persistence returns 503.
# Text-only prototype: DETAILS fits <=1000 characters AND <=1000 UTF-8 bytes,
# matching conservative existing Oracle VARCHAR2(1000 BYTE) capacity. The frontend
# asks the customer to shorten replies if the storage limit is exceeded.
# No document upload or attachment field has been introduced.
#
# UI / MANUAL HAPPY PATH
# 1. Officer opens an UNDER_REVIEW request, chooses Request more information and
#    enters a specific question (e.g. "Please clarify why you wish to exit.").
# 2. Borrower opens the same request: status More Information Required, officer
#    question visible under Additional Information, editable response form.
# 3. Borrower enters a clarification and clicks Submit for Review once.
# 4. Same request becomes UNDER_REVIEW; form disappears; full conversation remains.
# 5. Assigned officer opens the SAME exit request ID (not just the same borrower).
#    In an already-open modal, click Refresh Conversation or Refresh Status:
#    both refresh request status, conversation, list and summary. The reply is
#    visible and UNDER_REVIEW restores the assigned officer's decision form.
#    Use the EXISTING decision operation to approve, reject, or request
#    another round of information. No reassignment step is needed.
# 6. Only after approval can borrower accept a settlement quote and proceed to
#    payment/final completion using the existing checks. A grievance resolution
#    does not automatically approve the request or unlock payment.
# 7. Original request timing remains unchanged: a timely original submission can
#    still be reviewed later under existing officer policy; resubmission does not
#    create a new request or extend the quote/payment deadline.
# A legacy seeded MORE_INFO_REQUIRED request may have no question audit record.
# The UI says no specific remarks were recorded and still allows clarification;
# it does not invent an officer question or create another exit request.
#
# NEGATIVE / REPEAT TESTS (run manually)
# Missing JWT -> 401; officer JWT on borrower POST -> denied.
# Borrower B reading/responding to Borrower A's request -> 404, no audit/status write.
# Officer assigned to a different request -> history denied by existing visibility.
# Empty/whitespace/>1000-character/>1000-byte reply -> 400, unchanged state.
# Two simultaneous submissions -> one reply + UNDER_REVIEW; the other -> 409.
# Submission for UNDER_REVIEW/APPROVED/REJECTED/CANCELLED/COMPLETED -> 409.
# Inactive/closed loan or missing assigned officer -> 409, unchanged state.
# Request with accepted/paid quote or SUCCESS payment -> 409, bank review needed.
# Another officer request for information after resubmission -> another genuine
# question/reply round in chronological history, same request and officer.
# Keep request A open in the officer modal while the borrower replies to A;
# Refresh Conversation must show that reply and restore the decision form.
# Replying to request B must not change A's status or show B's messages in A.
# Original dates/reason/officer must be identical before and after resubmission;
# DECIDED_AT is null until the next officer decision. No loan/quote/payment writes.
# On an uncertain network result, refresh request status before submitting again.
#
# READ-ONLY ORACLE CHECKS (paste into SQL Developer; example request 21)
# SELECT EXIT_REQUEST_ID, LOAN_ID, OFFICER_ID, STATUS, REASON, REQUEST_DATE,
#        EXPIRY_DATE, DECIDED_AT, CREATED_AT, UPDATED_AT
# FROM COOLING_OFF_REQUEST WHERE EXIT_REQUEST_ID = 21;
# SELECT LOG_ID, USER_ID, OFFICER_ID, ACTION, DETAILS, ACTION_TIME
# FROM AUDIT_LOG WHERE EXIT_REQUEST_ID = 21
# AND ENTITY_TYPE = 'COOLING_OFF_REQUEST'
# AND ACTION IN ('COOLING_OFF_MORE_INFO_REQUIRED', 'COOLING_OFF_INFO_SUBMITTED')
# ORDER BY ACTION_TIME, LOG_ID;

@gateway = http://localhost:8080
@requestId = 21
@borrowerToken = REPLACE_WITH_BORROWER_JWT
@officerToken = REPLACE_WITH_ASSIGNED_LOAN_CLOSURE_OFFICER_JWT

### Borrower: read only the request's clarification conversation
GET {{gateway}}/api/cooling-off/requests/{{requestId}}/information-history
Authorization: Bearer {{borrowerToken}}

### Borrower: reply and return the SAME request to UNDER_REVIEW
POST {{gateway}}/api/cooling-off/requests/{{requestId}}/additional-information
Authorization: Bearer {{borrowerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"response": "The planned purchase was cancelled, so I no longer require this loan."}

### Officer: read the clarification and make a decision through the existing UI
GET {{gateway}}/api/officer/cooling-off/requests/{{requestId}}/information-history
Authorization: Bearer {{officerToken}}
